    "explanation": "Both parties: the disputed SGD 4.50 is the no-show cancellation fee charged on TRP-02722 (EV-FARE-02722: cancellation_fee 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). It is refunded in full, and no driver compensation is payable.\n\nThe fee fails the arrival test. POL-NS-01 makes a no-show fee chargeable only if all four of its conditions hold. Limb (a) holds - the trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 19:11:37 - and limb (d) holds - the trip was terminated by the driver at 19:18:19 under RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding. Limbs (b) and (c) fail on the trip's own trace. Run POL-NS-02's test on EV-GPS-02722 (weight 1.0, 100.0% coverage, max_gap_sec 0.0, both tracks present, 100 driver fixes at a 10 s cadence): qualifying_fix_count is 0 and the longest qualifying in-radius run is 0 fixes lasting 0.0 seconds, so no reading within the 50 m arrival radius for this STANDARD pickup met the 25 m accuracy filter for the required three consecutive fixes. POL-NS-01(b) therefore fails and the fee is not chargeable. Limb (c) fails for the same reason: POL-NS-01(c) measures dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not from the driver's tap, so the 402 seconds (about 6.7 minutes) between the 19:11:37 tap and the 19:18:19 cancellation is not dwell. The measured dwell is 0 seconds against the 180 seconds in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec), a shortfall of 180 seconds. POL-NS-06 then refunds the fee in full 'whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded to messages', and the fare breakdown charges nothing but that fee (base, distance, time, platform and waiting-time lines all at 0.00).\n\nThe driver's points. The arrival event, the RIDER_NO_SHOW code and the 180-second period are accepted (the 300-second figure in the fee schedule's legacy minimum-dwell table does not apply to a record that carries its own platform_policy block), but limbs (a) and (d) are necessary and not sufficient. The platform's wait timer does not carry arrival for this trip: it started two seconds after the driver's own tap and records only that the platform clock ran; POL-NS-12, the clause that lets the platform's arrival and wait events stand independently of the export, applies only where arrival_marker is GPS_AUTO, and this trip's marker is BUTTON - and the events state no geofence measurement and include no wait_timer_expired event in any case. The driver's statement 'I was at the pin for over six minutes' and his 19:11:57 message 'im at the pickup point' are his own assertions of position; an arrival tap and a message record only that he set and sent them, and neither can supply the three consecutive admissible in-radius fixes POL-NS-02 requires. The trace's summary does report a minimum driver-to-pin distance of 0.0 m, but that is a nearest-fix reading; fixes failing the 25 m accuracy filter count as evidence of neither presence nor absence, and the policy's own computed arrival test returns no qualifying run, so it does not rescue the fee. The rider's own position (891.7 to 898.7 m from the pin, stationary) and silence are accepted, and POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider - but POL-NS-01 has no rider-presence limb and POL-NS-06 makes the refund independent of it, so this does not help the driver. POL-NS-03 adds no compensation here: the record shows no stationary dwell within 400 m of the pin, and the clause's goodwill payment requires 2 or more registered pickup points while this trip records 1. The compensation figure of SGD 3.60 (80 percent of the SGD 4.50 net fee, from EV-FARE-02722's money block) and the anti-farming test are read correctly - no_show_terminations_30d 1 against completed_trips_30d 130, a rate of 0.008, below the 4-and-0.08 thresholds, and no other profile field may be used - but POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-06 does displace it.\n\nEscalation under POL-NS-09(b) is rejected: there are not two admissible artifacts contradicting each other directly on arrival. The trip record's arrival entry is a driver's tap, and POL-NS-12 excludes a BUTTON marker from carrying arrival, so the only artifact speaking to the driver's position is the trace, and its computed arrival result is one-way, not two. POL-NS-05 cannot be run on this record because the derived facts report no distance and no speed at the 19:11:37 marker; for that reason no false-arrival record is added under POL-NS-05(ii) either, and the refund does not need it, because POL-NS-02 decides the fee on the trace alone. No limb (a) to (e) of POL-NS-09 fires.\n\nIntegrity and confidence. No carrier of a deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08's limbs: the trace has no gap (max_gap_sec 0.0, 100 fixes at 10 s), the chat log's single message matches trip_record.chat_message_count of 1, and the fare line of 4.50 equals the net fee the resolution rule produces. EV-ADVIS-02722-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT); a missing artifact carries no fact, so it does not lower the confidence cap - it only makes POL-NS-06(i) accumulation unavailable, which nothing here needs. Confidence is capped at 1.0, the weight of EV-GPS-02722 and EV-FARE-02722, which carry the deciding facts, and is set at 0.90.\n\nOutcome: the rider's contested SGD 4.50 is refunded in full; no driver compensation is payable; no clause produces a referral on these facts. The monetary effect (SGD 4.50) is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so the refund executes on issue, and either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
